{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>If the sun has risen, he shall make full restitution.</b> The verse returns to the verse above, \"he shall restore five oxen\" etc. (above 21:37), like \"to a foreign people\" (ibid. 8), and likewise \"and so you shall do for your maidservant\" (Deut. 15:17), for it returns to the verse above it, \"you shall furnish him liberally\" (ibid. 14)." "<b>And he shall be sold for his theft.</b> On account of his theft."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Resolved the verse citation 'לעם נכרי (שם שם ח)' as Exodus 22:8 based on שם שם referring to the same chapter and verse sequence."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:37:17.863019538Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}